    fullDescription: "Bangla Road is the throbbing heart of Phuket's nightlife and one of the most famous party streets in Asia — a sensory overload of neon, noise and non-stop energy that has to be seen at least once, whether or not it is your scene. By day it is an unremarkable Patong street, but each evening around eight o'clock it closes to traffic and detonates into life: a 400-metre pedestrian strip crammed with open-fronted beer bars, thumping nightclubs, live-music venues, go-go bars, rooftop lounges and street performers, all competing in a blaze of flashing lights and pounding sound. Ping-pong-ball games, fire shows, costumed characters, tuk-tuks and touts add to the carnival chaos, and the whole street heaves with a boisterous international crowd until the early hours. It is loud, unashamedly hedonistic and occasionally seedy — the go-go bars and adult venues along the side sois are part of the landscape — but it is also, at surface level, a genuinely fun and free spectacle that many visitors enjoy simply strolling through, drink in hand, to take in the sheer spectacle. Sensible precautions apply: watch your belongings, agree the price of drinks and any 'shows' before committing, avoid the scams and overpriced side-bar traps, and keep an eye on how much you spend. Families with children usually give it a miss or pass through early. Love it or loathe it, Bangla Road is an inescapable part of the Phuket story and, for a certain kind of night out, unbeatable.",
