    fullDescription: "Lock Tien is a beloved old-school food court in the heart of Old Phuket Town, and it offers one of the best and most affordable introductions to the island's distinctive local hawker food, served from a cluster of long-established family stalls gathered under one open-air roof. This is where locals have come for generations to eat Phuket's signature dishes, and it remains refreshingly unpretentious, cheap and authentic — a world away from the resort restaurants. You order from the individual vendors, each specialising in their own dish, and eat at shared tables in the middle. The must-tries reflect Phuket's unique Hokkien-Chinese-influenced Baba cuisine: Hokkien fried noodles (a local staple), loba (a plate of deep-fried pork offal and tofu with a dipping sauce), po piah (fresh spring rolls), satay, curried noodles and, to finish, the famous o-aew — a refreshing local dessert of jelly, red beans and shaved ice that is a Phuket original. Portions are small and prices tiny, so the joy is in grazing across several stalls to sample a spread of specialities for very little money. It is cash only, busiest around lunchtime, and some stalls sell out and close by mid-afternoon, so going earlier in the day is best. The atmosphere is bustling, local and genuine. For budget-conscious and food-curious travellers wanting to taste real Phuket cooking cheaply and authentically while exploring the historic quarter, Lock Tien is an essential and delicious stop.",
