    fullDescription: "The neighbouring province of Krabi, across the bay to the east of Phuket, boasts some of the most spectacular coastal scenery in Thailand, and while it is a destination in its own right, its highlights can be sampled on a long but rewarding day trip from Phuket. The star attractions are the dramatic limestone karsts that soar out of the sea and along the shore, the beautiful beaches, and above all the Railay peninsula — a stunning stretch of coast so hemmed in by towering cliffs that it is cut off from the mainland by land and reachable only by boat, giving it a magical, secluded island feel. Railay's gorgeous white-sand beaches, backed by sheer jungle-topped cliffs that are world-renowned for rock climbing, and its hidden lagoons and caves, make it a jaw-dropping spot to explore. The other classic Krabi experience is the hugely popular 'Four Islands' tour, a longtail or speedboat trip that takes in Phra Nang Cave Beach, Chicken Island, Tup Island and Poda Island, with excellent snorkelling, swimming and, at low tide, a magical sandbar that emerges to connect several islands so you can walk between them across the sea. Reaching Krabi from Phuket takes a couple of hours by a combination of road and boat, so organised day tours that handle the logistics are the easiest way to do it in a day, though the distance means an early start and a full day out. Given its beauty, many travellers choose to stay a night or two in Krabi or on Railay to explore properly. For a scenic, karst-and-beach-filled day showcasing a different, equally beautiful corner of the Andaman coast, a Krabi and Railay trip is a superb choice.",
