    fullDescription: "Coral Island, known in Thai as Koh Hae, is the closest of Phuket's satellite islands and the ideal choice for those wanting a quick, easy and relaxed taste of the Thai-island experience without committing to a long full-day boat expedition. Lying just a short fifteen-minute speedboat hop off the south coast near Chalong, it is superbly accessible, making it perfect for a half-day trip, for families with young children, or for anyone short on time. As its English name suggests, the island is fringed by coral reefs in clear, shallow, calm water, and its two main beaches — Long Beach and Banana Beach — offer good, accessible snorkelling straight off the soft sand, with plenty of colourful reef fish to see close to shore. Beyond snorkelling, the island is well set up for an active, fun day by the water, with a range of optional watersports on offer, including banana-boat rides, kayaking, parasailing and the popular novelty of 'sea walking' (helmet diving that lets non-swimmers walk on the seabed among the fish). Alternatively, you can simply hire a sun lounger, swim in the warm, gentle sea and relax on the beach, with beach restaurants and bars on hand for lunch and drinks. Because it is so close and accessible, the island can get busy around the middle of the day when the tour boats converge, so a half-day trip timed for the earlier morning or the later afternoon offers a more peaceful experience. Easy, inexpensive, close and family-friendly, a Coral Island trip is the perfect introduction to island-hopping and a great option when you want beach and snorkelling fun with minimal travel and fuss.",
