    fullDescription: "Grab, Southeast Asia's dominant ride-hailing app, operates across Phuket and is comfortably the easiest, most transparent and often cheapest way for visitors to get around the island, removing the stress of negotiating with taxi and tuk-tuk drivers. Working just like Uber, the app lets you set your pickup point and destination, shows you the fixed fare upfront before you book (so there are no nasty surprises or haggling), matches you with a nearby driver, and lets you pay by cash or a linked card. Fares are generally very reasonable and considerably lower than the notoriously overpriced local taxis and tuk-tuks, with short local hops costing perhaps 80 to 150 baht and longer cross-island journeys between beaches or into town running from a couple of hundred baht upwards. It is well worth downloading the app and setting it up before you arrive. There are some caveats to be aware of, however. Because of long-standing tensions with the entrenched local taxi and tuk-tuk cartels, who have historically been hostile to app-based competition, Grab availability can be patchy in certain areas and at certain times — you may find fewer cars, longer waits or higher surge prices in some tourist hotspots, at busy beaches, late at night, or when demand is high, and some drivers prefer to meet you slightly away from taxi ranks to avoid confrontation. Despite these occasional frustrations, Grab remains the go-to choice for most independent travellers for its convenience, fixed pricing and cashless option, and it is generally reliable for getting between beaches, to and from the airport, into Phuket Town, and to restaurants and attractions. For getting around Phuket with minimal hassle and fair prices, Grab is invaluable.",
